Subject: [PATCH] emote: reactive "Siri-style" waveform face + `face` CLI demo

New headline display visual (DISPLAY_UX_PLAN § Phase 5). A runtime-drawn
waveform replaces the static emote eye while active — pure motion, no face:
  IDLE      calm breathing centre line
  LISTENING amplitude bars reacting to mic RMS
  THINKING  traveling scan pulse (no audio)
  SPEAKING  amplitude bars reacting to output RMS
Palette: hot core #FFE25E / accent #F5870B on true black, eased for fluidity.

The emote_gfx widget set has NO vector primitives (only label/anim/img/qrcode),
so each frame is rasterised into a PSRAM RGB565A8 strip (466x120, double-
buffered, ~328 KB) and pushed to a gfx image object via gfx_img_set_src(), which
invalidates → the engine repaints at its fps. A 20 fps FreeRTOS task eases
displayed amplitude toward target. Verified against the live decoder: C-array
magic 0x19, header.w/h/cf read from the dsc, RGB565A8 alpha plane at w*h*2.

CRITICAL — cameraless verification: the board has no camera, so a `face` CLI
command drives each state with a SYNTHETIC amplitude so the user can watch each
state on the AMOLED without a Gemini session:
  face off | idle | think
  face listen [pct]  | face speak [pct]   (pct 0-100; omitted = sinusoidal sweep)

Audio source is pluggable: emote_face_set_amplitude_source(cb) registers voice-
eng's live mic/out RMS getters; emote_face_set_synthetic_amplitude(milli) feeds
the CLI demo. Patch 0032 (later) wires the live getters — this patch is
self-contained on synthetic amplitude so the visual validates immediately.

Files (applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh apply_reactive_waveform_face_patch):
  + components/common/emote/waveform.c            (new — the renderer + task)
  ~ components/common/emote/include/emote.h        (face API + enum)
  ~ components/common/emote/emote.c                (call emote_face_init in start)
  ~ components/common/emote/CMakeLists.txt         (add waveform.c to SRCS)
  ~ components/common/app_claw/app_claw_cli.c      (the `face` command, emote-gated)

The mascot/HUD composite (§ Phase 2B) is demoted to the optional fallback — see
the plan. mascot-eng's 5 disc .eaf remain valid as the "face off" aesthetic.
